<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90846" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῠτᾰν-εία</span></b>  (A), 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῠτᾰν-ηΐη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>presidency</i>, at Athens the period during which the
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρυτάνεις</span> of each <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλή</span> in turn presided in the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλή</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκλησία</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				6.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.73
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑνδεκάτῃ τῆς
			πρυτανείας</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς
			Πανδιονίδος</span>) Decr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.27
			</span></i>, cf. Lex ib.<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.57.53
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				22.212.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				223
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				4
			</span></i>, al.: also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ πρυτανείαν</span>
			by <i>presidencies</i>, i.e. every <i><span class="en">
				35
			</span></i> or <i><span class="en">
				36
			</span></i> days, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				30.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				59.27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ γραμματεὺς ὁ κατὰ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.120.16
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽ ἑκάστην π</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>office</i> or <i>government of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρυτάνεις</span>, at Miletus, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1305a17
			</span></i>; at Rhodes, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.813d
			</span></i> (pl.); at Halicarnassus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1015.2
			</span></i>; at Mytilene, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).68
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>any public office held by rotation</i> for given periods;
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῆς ἡμέρης</span> the <i>chief
				command</i> for the day, held by each general in turn, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.110
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
